{"book":10,"chapter":14,"context":{"chapter":14,"title":"Absalom Brought Home","summary":"Joab sends a wise woman from Tekoa to tell David a made-up story that leads him to bring Absalom home. Absalom returns but is barred from the king's presence for two years, until he forces Joab's hand by setting his field on fire. David finally receives him with a kiss.","background":"Tekoa was a village south of Bethlehem, later the hometown of the prophet Amos. The woman's story uses the law of the avenger of blood to win a ruling from the king, then turns it on him, much as Nathan did in chapter 12. Absalom was famous for his looks and his heavy hair (vv. 25–26).","customs":[{"term":"Feign thyself to be a mourner","verses":"14:2","note":"She dressed in mourning clothes and went without anointing oil so her story of loss would look real."}],"watchFor":["A story that draws the king into judging his own case (vv. 4–17).","'We must needs die, and are as water spilt on the ground' (v. 14).","The half-reconciliation (v. 24) and the delayed kiss (v. 33)."],"connections":["Numbers 35:19","2 Samuel 12:1-7","2 Samuel 18:9","Amos 1:1"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיֵּדַע","vaiyeda'","H3045","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he perceived"],["יוֹאָב","yo'av","H3097","HNpm","Joab"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["צְרֻיָה","tzeruyah","H6870","HNpf","Zeruiah"],["כִּי","ki-","H3588","HTc","that"],["לֵב","lev","H3820","HNcmsc","[the] heart of"],["הַמֶּלֶךְ","hamelekh","H4428","HTd/Ncmsa","the king"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","[was] towards"],["אַבְשָׁלוֹם","'avshalom","H53","HNpm","Absalom"]],"x":[[10013039,10013039,5],[10002018,10002018,3]],"xn":2},"2":{"w":[["וַיִּשְׁלַח","vaiyishlach","H7971","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he sent"],["יוֹאָב","yo'av","H3097","HNpm","Joab"],["תְּקוֹעָה","teko'ah","H8620","HNpl/Sd","Tekoa towards"],["וַיִּקַּח","vaiyikach","H3947","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he took"],["מִשָּׁם","misham","H8033","HR/D","from there"],["אִשָּׁה","'ishah","H802","HNcfsa","a woman"],["חֲכָמָה","chakhamah"